# Independent Flow/Vault historical proof transition review

The exact22-file root transition candidate is accepted for its finite source-only contract. This review does not install anything or execute application, original product, browser, full-suite, benchmark or whole-root publication verification. Studio and the frozen authorities remain unchanged.

Ten check groups pass, including177 fresh rejection controls. All609 captured source rows are exact before/after. The actual candidate library is constructed96 times: one accepted virtual baseline;88 mutated/missing mandatory source attempts; five accepted constructions with subsequently changed input rejected on final summary; and two invalid reader attempts. These are source-proof library evaluations, not product executions.

Five exact inverse transformations recover the installed26,303-byte prior migration module. The old fixed identities and unchanged filesystem adapter are exact. The new candidate47,841-byte module is SHA3d0a4ee0b5e9eef36c357c9a3c6170008a2bb0882cc8a755756358aabdf6ced1. The virtual reader overlays only35 independently accepted proposed files and12 exact candidate authority/before/metadata aliases. All other proof inputs come from the current public repository. No files are substituted by a broad SHA fallback.

The accepted initial source-proof library authenticates106 files/3,431,611 bytes. Its required current union is61 files (26 prior unchanged plus35 latest). Nine current before-images are authenticated. Four replaced prior Vault after-images remain mandatory historical bytes, while the new current files are independently mandatory. Seven external current verifiers and their exact old before-images remain mandatory. The old847/720/727 capsule and the old937/737/753 capsule remain historical, with four selected937 source/attempt/development inputs and a frozen prior STATUS before-image. New current acceptance is not inferred from either historical suite.

The distinct named source path union is13; it comprises9 changed code paths in the old720 census and4 documentation paths outside that census. Old intermediate identities, latest before/after identities and older before-images resolve only through the exact named route. Unknown paths return no mapping; unsafe paths and malformed expected identities reject. Fresh checks mutate every61 current file, every7 external verifier, both authority declarations, all9 before-images and later settled sources. Signed conclusions and labels are unchanged; there is no full product parity or superiority claim.

Bounds are160 distinct authenticated files,16MiB aggregate authenticated bytes and32MiB per Buffer read. The raw-reader interface receives a Buffer before checking bounds, so it cannot prevent an external reader's preallocation. The unchanged filesystem adapter inspects segment links, real paths and file size before reading and rereads identities through summary. Those checks do not create an atomic filesystem snapshot or eliminate Windows filesystem races. The explicit virtual reader was used in this campaign; no new filesystem-race acceptance is asserted.

Whole-root execution was considered but deferred: the current PUBLICATION-MANIFEST pins pre-installation active files. This review does not create a speculative future publication manifest, invent a development receipt, bypass publication checks or label an adapted root run unchanged. Root owns actual installation, new source-bound app suites, publication regeneration and final whole-root integrity.

The complete22-authority epoch, accepted Flow67 and accepted Vault72 independent review epochs were strictly authenticated. Their selected manifests/receipts and exact candidate/inverse records are copied inertly into authority/; no recursive payload/history copy or native original artifact is included. The final independent collector completed on its first execution with zero collector failures. Raw source-proof calls and all177 refusals are retained.
